  "evidence_notes": "Robert, 61, was diagnosed with Crohn's five years ago, but likely had it longer. He also has COPD and peripheral neuropathy. He experienced misdiagnosis for years before his Crohn's diagnosis at 56. He started with mesalamine, then budesonide, and then azathioprine, which caused liver issues. Methotrexate caused unbearable fatigue. He initially resisted biologics due to lung disease but started Remicade a year ago, which has shown noticeable improvement. He is dealing with neuropathy, restricted diet, and the impact of his illness on his retirement and family. He is discussing adding an immunomodulator to Remicade."
